        text: 'The NRO precedent defeats the strongest a priori objection to a concealed legacy program - that \'someone would have talked\'. Reasoning: an agency with tens of thousands of cleared personnel and a multi-billion-dollar annual budget sustained total public non-existence for 31 years, so the leak-rate argument is empirically falsified.',
        source: 'Inference from the documented 1961-1992 concealment of the NRO\'s existence'
