    tierRationale: 'Re-graded A on a global pass (rank 45 of 956, score 79). 13 connections, 1 of them custody/witness/funding/programmatic, 4 official denials recorded against it. Axes C1/A3/D3.',
    claims: [
      {
        tier: 1,
        text: 'A full-text search of the released AARO Historical Record Report Volume I returns no occurrence of \'Yankee Blue\'. The term is likewise absent from the FY2023, FY2024 and FY2025 consolidated annual reports.',
        source: 'AARO HRR Vol I, March 2024, full text; AARO annual reports FY2023-FY2025'
      },
      {
        tier: 3,
        text: 'The claim that AARO acknowledged Yankee Blue in Volume I is widely repeated in reporting and was asserted on this board until 12 Aug 2026. It does not survive a full-text check of the document.',
        source: 'Correction logged 12 Aug 2026; see notes/WAVE3_QUEUE.md'
      },
      {
        tier: 3,
        text: 'Yankee Blue therefore has no Tier 1 anchor in the AARO documentary record as of 12 Aug 2026. The public account rests on June 2025 press reporting and on statements attributed to AARO officials describing an Air Force hazing/indoctrination practice at Kirtland AFB in which personnel were falsely read into a non-existent UAP program; the underlying memo has not been released. Reasoning: direct full-text verification against the only AARO report that could plausibly have contained it, plus the absence of any Yankee Blue reference in the FY2023, FY2024 and FY2025 annual reports (also searched, zero hits).',
        source: 'https://media.defense.gov/2024/Mar/08/2003409233/-1/-1/0/DOPSR-CLEARED-508-COMPLIANT-HRRV1-08-MAR-2024-FINAL.PDF'
      },
      {
        tier: 1,
        text: 'OSD\'s final response in FOIA case 25-F-3514 (September 2025) stated that after \'thorough searches of the electronic records and files of CMD, no records of the kind you described could be identified\' regarding the alleged spring 2023 cessation memo.',
        source: 'OSD FOIA response, case 25-F-3514, September 2025'
      },
      {
        tier: 1,
        text: 'On 1 October 2025 Pentagon spokesperson Susan Gough stated: \'Regarding the alleged memo: I cannot confirm the existence of any department-level memo as described in the article. You may want to ask the Air Force or other military services whether they put out such a memo to their personnel.\'',
        source: 'Susan Gough, Department of War, statement of 1 Oct 2025'
      },
      {
        tier: 1,
        text: 'On 15 December 2025 a FOIA appellate decision remanded the case to the Department for additional searches, granting the appeal that argued a search limited to the Correspondence Management Division was inadequate under Oglesby v. U.S. Dep\'t of Army, 920 F.2d 57 (D.C. Cir. 1990).',
        source: 'Department of War FOIA appellate decision, December 2025'
      },
      {
        tier: 2,
        text: 'The Wall Street Journal reported in June 2025 that the practice convinced \'hundreds and hundreds of people\' they were working on a reverse-engineering programme for alien technology, and that DNI Avril Haines was briefed and described as stunned.',
        source: 'Wall Street Journal reporting, June 2025, as summarised in FOIA appeal filings'
      },
      {
        tier: 2,
        text: 'Air Force personnel in classified units were briefed into a fictitious programme called Yankee Blue involving reverse-engineering of alien spacecraft, shown flying-saucer photographs, bound by NDAs, and in some accounts threatened with severe penalties for disclosure.',
        source: 'Wall Street Journal investigation, 6 June 2025'
      },
      {
        tier: 2,
        text: 'The Office of the Secretary of Defense issued a memorandum in spring 2023 ordering the practice halted immediately.',
        source: 'Wall Street Journal, 6 June 2025'
      },
      {
        tier: 2,
        text: 'Officials briefed DNI Avril Haines that \'hundreds and hundreds\' of personnel had been affected over decades.',
        source: 'Wall Street Journal, 6 June 2025'
      },
      {
        tier: 2,
        text: 'A DoD spokeswoman confirmed the findings were not complete when Volume I was released and would appear in Volume II of the Historical Record Report, then scheduled for late 2025.',
        source: 'DoD spokeswoman Susan Gough to the Wall Street Journal, June 2025'
      },
      {
        tier: 1,
        text: 'AARO\'s Historical Record Report Volume I states that AARO found \'no NDAs that contain information related to UAP.\'',
        source: 'AARO Historical Record Report Volume I, February 2024, p.30'
      },
      {
        tier: 3,
        text: 'The Volume I NDA finding and the Yankee Blue NDA record are irreconcilable as written; either Volume I\'s search was scoped to exclude the practice, or the practice was not disclosed to the drafters, or the finding was knowingly narrow.',
        source: 'Inference from the direct textual conflict between Volume I p.30 and the Department\'s own confirmed account of Yankee Blue NDAs'
      }
    ],
