        text: 'Section 1687 does not repeal or amend 10 U.S.C. 119(e). It operates on appropriations instead: the waiver remains lawful, but funds in the FY2024 Act cannot be spent on a UAP-related special- or restricted-access activity that has not been detailed to the wider list. The legal question it creates is therefore an Antideficiency/appropriations question about a specific fiscal year\'s money, not a classification question. Reasoning stated from the text of 1687(a) and 119(e).',
