    id: 'iaa-fy2024-sec1104',
    cls: 'legislation',
    label: 'S. 2103 Sec. 1104 - SSCI contractor disclosure and immunity provision (stripped)',
    cluster: 'oversight',
    sub: 'Reported-but-not-enacted requirement that contractors surrender non-earth origin material',
    desc: 'On 22 June 2023 Senator Mark Warner reported S. 2103, the Intelligence Authorization Act for Fiscal Year 2024, from the Select Committee on Intelligence. Section 1104 is the most explicit statement any organ of the US government has made about private custody of non-terrestrial material. Subsection (d) requires that \'any person currently or formerly under contract with the Federal Government that has in their possession material or information provided by or derived from the Federal Government relating to unidentified anomalous phenomena that formerly or currently is protected by any form of special access or restricted access\' notify the Director of National Intelligence within 60 days and, within 180 days, make available for assessment, analysis and inspection all such material and information plus \'a comprehensive list of all non-earth origin or exotic unidentified anomalous phenomena material.\' Subsection (e) grants immunity: \'No criminal or civil action may lie or be maintained in any Federal or State court against any person for receiving material or information described in subsection (d) if that person complies.\' Subsection (c) lists the activities to be defunded absent disclosure: recovering and securing UAP craft, analysing craft for reverse engineering, and developing propulsion derived from recovered craft. The Senate Intelligence Committee approved this unanimously. None of subsections (d) through (g) survived into the enacted law; only the funding limitation and the IR&D restriction did.',
