    id: 'sec-8009-sap-notice',
    cls: 'legislation',
    label: 'Section 8009 - 30-day advance notice before initiating or materially modifying a special access program',
    cluster: 'oversight',
    sub: 'Appropriations-side SAP tripwire; the companion to 10 U.S.C. 119',
    desc: 'Section 8009 of the Department of Defense Appropriations Act for fiscal year 2026 provides, in a single sentence: \'Funds appropriated by this Act may not be used to initiate, or materially modify the scope of, a special access program without prior notification 30 calendar days in advance to the congressional defense committees.\' It is the appropriations-side companion to the authorisation-side reporting regime of 10 U.S.C. 119, and it is a purer instrument, because it attaches to the money rather than to a reporting duty and because it contains no waiver. A programme initiated with funds appropriated by that Act without the 30-day notice is a programme operating on funds the statute says may not be used for it. This is the provision against which any concealed UAP-related special access programme would have to be measured, and it is also the provision that a programme predating 1988 - or funded from sources other than annual DoD appropriations, such as contractor IR&D reimbursement or the CIA\'s unvouchered account under 50 U.S.C. 3510 - would not touch at all.',
