        text: 'Claussen: a US cargo mission of this kind \'would require paperwork from Air Mobility Command at Scott AFB in Illinois and the Air Mobility Wing at Charleston AFB in South Carolina\', plus refuelling records and an international flight plan; Brazilian air traffic controller Marco Feres reported that on or about 20 January 1996 a USAF cargo aircraft, most likely a C-17, landed at Viracopos airport in Campinas to collect an unusual cargo.',
